# cabin_fog_low: the fog's low band (BUILD_PLAN S7, 5.8): chains of
# overlapping rounded puffs, the vapour's light over its shade (snow over
# glacier blue by day and at dawn), solid, its top and its foot lobed and
# its ends rounded inside the frame, so it never stops as a square block at
# an edge. Only where it can show: web/js/gfx/cabin.js draws it at
# at_fog_low, in the mid layer behind the maples, the spruce and the shed
# and in front of the forest wall and the conifers, so it lies across the
# forest wall's top under the left maple and behind its trunk, and above
# the shed behind the right maple's trunk (the cabin hides the valley floor
# between); the trunks and the cabin stay crisp in front of it. At the
# plate's origin.
